        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
          <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">One of Dubai’s key advantages as a financial centre is its legal structure. While the wider UAE follows a civil law system influenced by Sharia and continental legal traditions, the Dubai International Financial Centre (DIFC) operates under a framework based on common law principles. This gives many international investors and firms a more familiar environment for doing business.</p>
